<task id="205h" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration — row A38c (operator-script marker pre-check gates (A38c — closes rotation/seed/legacy-orchestrator reversal vectors))</title>
    <phase>Phase Pre-Live-Fire — Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration (task 205, A38c re-scope 2026-08-25)</phase>
    <gate>ready</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Per project CLAUDE.md rigor table + root CLAUDE.md §8 TEST-MODIFYING/auth override: A38c is the OPERATOR-SCRIPT half of the A38 re-scope (peer-escalated 2026-08-25 `partial-omit-set-discovered`; owner approved). It gates three operator entry points (`Rotate-Secrets.ps1`, `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1`, `Provision-Customer.ps1`) that — verified live by task 205a's grep-inventory — would otherwise silently reverse the auth-v4 secret-free migration by re-minting `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` + `AiSearch--AdminKey` on every rotation/seed/legacy-orchestrator run while reporting green. Row is tagged `auth` (secret-management surface + FR-39 credential-selection seam), which triggers unconditional code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 per root CLAUDE.md §8 override; ADR-028 A4 rationale (secret-free BFF identity — per `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` APPROVED 2026-08-25) + §6.5 owner-narrowed disposition (prong 3 collapses to `spaarkedev1`; Q6 forbids new Model 2 stamps before A36-A42 land) must both be preserved by these gates.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical apply of a well-specified delta per peer escalation record (`notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` lines 76-99 "A38 execution record" + §"Proposed complete omit-set re-scope"): pattern is a marker-detection pre-check that either FAIL-LOUDs (secret-free marker present) or falls through to current write behavior (no marker). Same FAIL-LOUD shape as A43's `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` gate at `:617-660` (`-CutoverBffSettings` MI-check refusal) — mirror that precedent into three PowerShell operator scripts. No credential logic authoring, no cross-worktree consumption; PowerShell-only under `scripts/*.ps1`; three disjoint file surfaces; scoped mechanical change per §8.5 Sonnet-5 default. FULL rigor already provides the quality gate (code-review + adr-check unconditional per auth tag).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>PowerShell-only under scripts/*.ps1 (Rotate-Secrets.ps1 + Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1 + Provision-Customer.ps1); disjoint from 205a A38a (KvSecretsPopulation/**), 205b A42 (EntraAppReg/**), 205g A38b (infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep), 205i A44.5 (EnvVarValues/**), 205e A43 (scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>A35 (landed); loosely coordinated with A38a on marker-detection convention (A38a defines the KV tag key/value + sprk_dataverseenvironment state field)</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, auth, powershell, secret-free-gate, operator-scripts, marker-precheck</tags>
