  <prompt>Apply the OPERATOR-SCRIPT half of the A38 re-scope (row **A38c**, dispatched from task 205a's peer escalation record at `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` lines 76-99). Three PowerShell operator entry points, verified live by task 205a's grep-inventory, currently write auth-v4-retired credentials with NO secret-free gate — every rotation / operator seed / legacy-orchestrator run silently re-mints these secrets on secret-free envs while reporting green, undoing A38a (manifest omit) + A38b (Bicep gate) migration:

1. `scripts/Rotate-Secrets.ps1:588` (platform vault) + `:661` (per-customer vaults) — `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` rotation, no secret-free gate. (`BFF-API-ClientSecret` rotation is already a retired no-op at `:604-619` per auth-v4 task 033 ✓ — do NOT re-add that branch.)
2. `scripts/Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1:123` (`ServiceBus-ConnectionString`) + `:178` (`AiSearch--AdminKey`) — operator seeding writes, no secret-free gate. (`BFF-API-ClientSecret` seeding already REMOVED per auth-v4 task 033 ✓ — do NOT re-add.)
3. `scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1:533` — legacy 13-step orchestrator (superseded by L2 control-plane per §5.2) still writes `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` in the `$secrets` hashtable.

Row-shape: (a) grep-verify current state at each of the 5 call sites BEFORE editing (line numbers may have drifted since 2026-08-25); (b) add a marker pre-check gate BEFORE the write path at each site — detection reads KV resource tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity` (canonical key defined by A38a; use `# TODO(A38a): reconcile canonical tag value` placeholder if A38a still in-flight) OR `sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_credentialmode=secret-free` state field; (c) if marker present → FAIL LOUD with actionable message naming the marker + linking to the A38a omit contract (constraint file location + row number) + refusing to write; if no marker → keep current fallback behavior UNCHANGED (backwards compat for pre-migration envs); (d) for `Provision-Customer.ps1` (legacy orchestrator per §5.2), optionally add a deprecation banner in addition to the gate; (e) preserve script idempotency (re-runs against a secret-free env stay safe — refuse consistently, no partial writes); (f) MUST use same marker convention as A38a (single source of truth: A38a defines it, A38c/A43 consume it, A44 consumes it — do NOT invent a parallel convention); (g) MUST use FAIL-LOUD shape consistent with A43 (`Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` gate at `:617-660`); (h) MUST NOT touch `BFF-API-ClientSecret` rotation/seed paths (already retired per auth-v4 task 033) or Redis rotation (separate concern); (i) amend punch-list annotation `last_known_status_after_execution` on row A38c. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>PowerShell hardening specialist + auth-v4 secret-free credential-contract preserver + operator-script silent-failure gate author. Expert in: (a) the three operator entry points (`Rotate-Secrets.ps1` / `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` / `Provision-Customer.ps1`) and their current silent-write surfaces per task 205a's grep-verified inventory (lines 82-88 of the peer escalation record); (b) the auth-v4 secret-free credential contract per master ADR-028 A4 (verified via A35 merge) — MI-FIC default, KV cert fallback, NEVER re-mint retired secrets; (c) the §10.5 silent-fallback trap-class extended to operator scripts (rotation / seed / legacy-orchestrator = Δ1/Δ2 reversal disguised as green run); (d) the A43 precedent (`Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660` `-CutoverBffSettings` MI-check refusal) as the canonical FAIL-LOUD shape to mirror; (e) A38a's KV-tag marker contract (per §9.1: "positive migration marker = KV tag or provisioning-state field, never the credential slot") + `sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_credentialmode` state field as the SECONDARY signal; (f) the auth-v4 task 033 retirement facts (`BFF-API-ClientSecret` rotation is a no-op at `Rotate-Secrets.ps1:604-619`; seeding removed from `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` on 2026-08-24) — MUST preserve these as-is; (g) `Provision-Customer.ps1` §5.2 supersession by L2 control-plane (legacy 13-step orchestrator; deprecation banner is optional-but-recommended); (h) fleet-consistency invariants under Model 2 per-customer vaults (§10.3) — the gate MUST work identically across N vaults.</role>

  <goal>Row A38c annotated with `last_known_status_after_execution` in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`. Three PowerShell operator scripts gated at all 5 grep-verified call sites:

- `scripts/Rotate-Secrets.ps1` — `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` rotation branches at `:588` (platform vault) AND `:661` (per-customer vaults) gated on secret-free marker → FAIL LOUD (name marker + link A38a omit contract + refuse) OR skip cleanly; `:604-619` `BFF-API-ClientSecret` no-op branch untouched; Redis rotation untouched (separate concern).
- `scripts/Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` — `Set-VaultSecret` calls for `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` at `:123` AND `AiSearch--AdminKey` at `:178` gated on secret-free marker → FAIL LOUD OR skip cleanly; `BFF-API-ClientSecret` seed already REMOVED per auth-v4 task 033 — do NOT reintroduce.
- `scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1` — `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` write in `$secrets` hashtable at `:533` gated → FAIL LOUD OR skip cleanly; deprecation banner optionally added at script entry naming §5.2 L2 control-plane supersession.

All three scripts: FAIL-LOUD message actionable — names the marker (KV tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity` and/or `sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_credentialmode=secret-free`), links to A38a omit contract (`.claude/constraints/auth.md` + row A38a in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`), refuses to write (never a silent no-op that reports green). All three scripts: pre-migration envs (no marker) behave BYTE-IDENTICAL to pre-edit baseline (backwards compat unit-tested). Marker convention consistent with A38a (single source of truth — grep confirms same tag key/state field used across A38a + A38c + A43 + A44). Fleet-consistency (Model 2): gate works identically across N per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` vaults; documented inline. Integration tests OR manual smoke: run each of the three scripts against a mocked/marker-tagged secret-free env → refuses/fails-loud (grep asserts no `Set-VaultSecret` / `az keyvault secret set` call executed); run against a pre-migration env → current behavior preserved. Idempotency preserved: repeated runs against a secret-free env produce identical no-op behavior (no partial writes). All three scripts parse cleanly (`pwsh -NoProfile` syntax check succeeds).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Row A38c is one of three re-scoped sub-rows spawned by task 205a's ESCALATION 2026-08-25 (`partial-omit-set-discovered` trigger; see `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` lines 76-99). The original A38 row landed only in `Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/**` (manifest omit + handler seam); task 205a's grep-verify showed that the manifest omit alone would report "omitted/migrated" while the SAME provisioning run (H2a Bicep) + subsequent operator actions (Rotate-Secrets / Seed-ProductionKeyVault / Provision-Customer legacy path) would silently re-seed the retired secrets — the exact "falsely reports migrated" failure the trigger names. The re-scope splits A38 into: A38a (manifest/handler omit — original landing spot; 205a re-dispatched), A38b (Bicep gate at `customer.bicep`; 205g), A38c (operator-script marker pre-check gates — THIS ROW; 205h), and A44.5 (H7/task-142 half of A30's sentinel contract; 205i).

Task 205a's grep-verified live-site inventory (peer escalation record lines 82-88, cross-checked against remediation plan §5.3 bullet 3.2's "⚠️ analysis-only cites" list):

- Rotate-Secrets.ps1: SB rotation branches at `:588` (platform vault) + `:661` (per-customer vaults). `BFF-API-ClientSecret` rotation already a retired no-op at `:604-619` per auth-v4 task 033 ✓ (do NOT re-add).
- Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1: SB write at `:123` + AiSearch admin-key write at `:178`. `BFF-API-ClientSecret` seed already REMOVED 2026-08-24 per auth-v4 task 033 ✓ (do NOT re-add).
- Provision-Customer.ps1: SB conn string write in `$secrets` hashtable at `:533`. Legacy 13-step orchestrator superseded by L2 control-plane per §5.2 — deprecation banner optional.

Detection: read KV resource tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity` (canonical key defined by A38a — 205a is authoring the manifest/handler seam at task 205a-refire) OR `sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_credentialmode=secret-free` state field. Same FAIL-LOUD shape as A43's `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660` (`-CutoverBffSettings` MI-check refusal). Under Model 2, N per-customer vaults each carry their own tag — the gate MUST work identically across N vaults per §10.3 fleet-consistency.

A38c depends on A35 (landed) because the ADR-028 A4 amendment governing "why these gates exist" arrived via the master merge — pre-A35 this worktree's ADR-028 had no A4. A38c is loosely coordinated with A38a on marker-detection convention: A38a is single-source-of-truth for the KV tag key/value AND the `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field name/values. If A38a landing is still in-flight at A38c dispatch time, A38c lands with `# TODO(A38a): reconcile canonical tag value` placeholder + reference to punch row A38a in comment — do NOT invent a divergent convention. A38c is a Pre-Phase-F gate rather than a 186-hard-blocker (task 186 does not itself run rotation), but strongly recommended in the same commit bundle as A38a + A38b for defense-in-depth (the three together close the complete omit-set per the peer escalation re-scope).

§6.5 owner-narrowed disposition (per `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` §"Owner refinements 2026-08-25"): prong 3 collapses to `spaarkedev1` only (no live prod exists; per Q6, no new Model 2 stamps before A36-A42 land); `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` + `Configure-ProductionAppSettings.ps1` are "aspirational-not-active until a real prod exists." A38c's gate on `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` MUST therefore be forward-looking: it enforces the correct behavior when prod comes online, not against a currently-active production estate. §6.5 also confirms `Dataverse-ClientSecret` is time-boxed Path A through 2026-11-23 — A38c gates ONLY the auth-v4-retired credentials (`ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`), NOT `Dataverse-ClientSecret` (which remains protected under narrow Path A through sunset).</background>
