  <notes>**Justification (root CLAUDE.md §11 three-question template)**: **Existing** — the A43 `-CutoverBffSettings` gate at `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660` (task 205e) established the FAIL-LOUD refusal shape; A38a (task 205a re-dispatched) establishes the KV-tag secret-free-marker canonical convention; auth-v4 task 033 established the `BFF-API-ClientSecret` retirement invariants at `Rotate-Secrets.ps1:604-619` no-op + `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` removed-seed. All three exist as precedents. **Extension** — A38c extends the A43 FAIL-LOUD shape to three additional operator entry points (`Rotate-Secrets.ps1` + `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` + `Provision-Customer.ps1`) that task 205a's grep-inventory (peer escalation record lines 82-88) verified as still silently re-minting retired secrets on secret-free envs. Adds a shared `Assert-SpaarkeSecretFreeGateNotTripped` helper to avoid drift across the three scripts. No new components beyond the shared helper; three single-file edits + tests. **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete failure modes per peer escalation record + remediation plan §5.3 bullet 3.2)** — (a) every rotation run of `Rotate-Secrets.ps1` against a secret-free env resurrects `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` at the platform vault (`:588`) AND at every per-customer vault (`:661`) — undoing A38a manifest omit + A38b Bicep gate migration; run reports green (rotation cadence typically hides this for weeks); (b) every operator invocation of `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` on a secret-free env resurrects `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` at `:123` + `AiSearch--AdminKey` at `:178` — same silent Δ1/Δ2 reversal (Δ2 reversal is the same trap class A43 gates in `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1`; A38c closes the operator-seed twin); (c) any legacy `Provision-Customer.ps1` run (13-step orchestrator per §5.2 supersession — should not happen post-L2, but the script exists and remains executable) writes `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` at `:533` before H2a even executes — the exact "falsely reports migrated" failure the original A38 escalation identified; (d) reversal vectors surface ONLY on drift audit — days or weeks later; the H0 preflight cannot catch them because the writes happen post-preflight, on operator-initiated schedules; (e) A38a + A38b land the manifest and Bicep halves of the omit but leave the operator-invoked half open — the three (A38a + A38b + A38c) together close the complete omit-set per the peer escalation re-scope, and landing them in the same commit bundle provides defense-in-depth; (f) A38c is a Pre-Phase-F gate rather than a 186-hard-blocker (task 186 does not itself run rotation), but strongly recommended in the same commit bundle for defense-in-depth — without it, the FIRST customer rotation post-186 silently reverses the migration.</notes>

